---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// DRAFT — "Recovering after" path. Intentionally a being-shaped placeholder: the
// source has no recovery steps yet. Do not fabricate steps. Honest invitation +
// cycle close back to "before".
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Recovering after | Workflows | Resilience Hub Toolkit"
  description="Recovering after a flood: the transition from response into long-term recovery. This path is being shaped with the team."
>
  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl">
      <nav class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/workflows" class="hover:text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Workflows</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span class="text-foreground">Recovering after</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-hero font-semibold mb-4 text-foreground">Recovering after</h1>
      <p class="text-body-large text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-8">
        The transition from active response into long-term recovery: working with
        long-term recovery groups, supporting households through the slow rebuild,
        and holding what the community learned.
      </p>

      <!-- Being-shaped panel: intentional invitation, not an apology -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border-t-4 border-t-secondary border border-border bg-card p-6 shadow-card">
        <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-secondary mb-2">Being shaped with the team</p>
        <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">This path is still being written</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground mb-3">
          The before and response paths grew out of work people had already done and
          written down. The recovery path is the one we are shaping next, with the
          people who have lived it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground">
          If you have carried a community through recovery and want to help shape
          this path, we would love your input. This is a draft, and it is open.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Cycle close -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted p-5 mt-8">
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground">
          Recovery is not the end of the line. What a community learns here, the
          relationships, the directories, the trained volunteers, becomes the
          capacity it carries into the next time it prepares. Recovery feeds the
          next <a href="/workflows/before" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">before</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <nav class="flex items-center justify-between border-t border-border mt-10 pt-6 text-body-small" aria-label="Path navigation">
        <a href="/workflows/response" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary underline underline-offset-2">&larr; Responding to a flood</a>
        <a href="/workflows" class="text-primary font-medium underline underline-offset-2">All workflows</a>
      </nav>

      <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mt-8">
        Shaped by the Resilience Hub Toolkit coalition, with RAFT VT, NEK Organizing,
        and CROs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
